{"schema_version":"1.0.0","metadata":{"trial_id":"202610080659-corner-cafe","prompting_method_id":"concept-build-free.v0","model_id":"claude-opus-5-5","seed":11,"server_state_id":"concept-free.v1"},"style":{"name":"sandstone market-house with oak shopfront and brick corner tower","rationale":"Second pass, judged as someone in the street would see it. Keep: the striped corner tower, the orange shutters, the terrace with orange/white awnings, the blue stall on the -x front and the sandstone pilasters. Fix 1, the tower: the old one had glass and was crowned with a wide brick 'mushroom'. It is now a solid 3x3 smooth-sandstone shaft standing 1 block proud of both fronts. It has cut-sandstone quoins, a sandstone_wall chamfer column (brick_wall at the bands) so the corner reads as rounded, and brick bands at y4-5, 8-9 and 12-13. Slit windows stack on the axis above the door. It rises 4 blocks clear of the parapet, then a one-step corbelled brick crown, a stepped brick_stairs cap and a cut-sandstone finial with a lantern. Fix 2, the facades: they read as loose columns. Every bay is now the same 3-wide module between 1-wide proud cut-sandstone pilasters with chiseled capitals. The module, bottom to top: a stone-brick plinth; double-height glass set back one block in an oak_fence mullion and transom grid; an oak band carrying a balcony slab and fence rail; a cobblestone spandrel; a recessed window between orange_terracotta shutters; a stripped-oak beam; an oak-clad top storey with a recessed window. Fix 3, the roofline: it was ragged. A continuous upside-down oak_stairs cornice now runs on all four sides. Above it sits an oak parapet with a slab cap, punctuated by cut-sandstone posts over each pilaster, plus the bakery-oven brick chimney and a roof hatch. Fix 4, the +x side: it was a large plain wall. It now has the same pilasters, sandstone bands, recessed windows and shutters, so the finished look carries round the corner. The back stays simple, with a door, bands and a few windows. Ground floor: the corner door sits in the tower under an oak canopy with fence lattice, a sign, pink and brown banners and hanging lanterns. The raised oak terrace has a stair entry, two chair-and-table sets with cakes and two striped awnings. The -x street has barrels, a composter, a blue-and-white produce stall and a hanging sign on a fence bracket. Lanterns hang under every balcony. Paving is cobblestone with a stone-brick edge."},"palette":{"manifest":["minecraft:cobblestone","minecraft:stone_bricks","minecraft:stone_brick_stairs","minecraft:oak_planks","minecraft:oak_slab","minecraft:oak_stairs","minecraft:oak_fence","minecraft:oak_door","minecraft:oak_trapdoor","minecraft:oak_wall_sign","minecraft:oak_hanging_sign","minecraft:stripped_oak_log","minecraft:glass_pane","minecraft:orange_terracotta","minecraft:smooth_sandstone","minecraft:cut_sandstone","minecraft:chiseled_sandstone","minecraft:sandstone_wall","minecraft:bricks","minecraft:brick_wall","minecraft:brick_stairs","minecraft:lantern","minecraft:pink_wall_banner","minecraft:brown_wall_banner","minecraft:potted_poppy","minecraft:potted_dandelion","minecraft:orange_wool","minecraft:white_wool","minecraft:light_blue_wool","minecraft:cake","minecraft:barrel","minecraft:composter","minecraft:pumpkin"]},"placements":[{"op":"fill","from":[-3,0,-3],"to":[15,0,15],"block":"minecraft:cobblestone"},{"op":"line","from":[-3,0,-3],"to":[15,0,-3],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"line","from":[-3,0,-3],"to":[-3,0,15],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"line","from":[15,0,-3],"to":[15,0,15],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"line","from":[-3,0,15],"to":[15,0,15],"block":"minecraft:stone_bricks"},{"op":"fill","from":[1,1,1],"to":[12,1,12],"block":"minecraft:oak_planks"},{"op":"fill","from":[1,6,1],"to":[12,6,12],"block":"minecraft:oak_planks"},{"op":"fill","from":[1,10,1],"to":[12,10,12],"block":"minecraft:oak_planks"},{"op":"fill","from":[1,13,1],"to":[12,13,12],"block":"minecraft:oak_planks